		(property "Note" "DVI decoupling for U3 (BH1750) - ROHM application circuit ex1 (datasheet Rev.C p.8, 'The control signal line such as CPU is connected'). DVI is NOT a plain interface supply: it is the asynchronous reset input, and the datasheet requires it held <=0.4V for >=1us AFTER VCC is established, otherwise 'ADDR, SDA, SCL is not stable'. It was previously strapped straight to VCC, giving a 0us reset section - and because SENSOR_3V3 is switched by Q3 that power-up sequence replays ~17500 times a year, not once at boot. Now driven by P1.12 (J1 pin 5). Distinct from C8, which is the VCC bypass; ex1 shows both. See github issue #21."
			(at 359.41 299.72 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
